<title>UK: Edge buys retail park for 11.75 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Edge buys retail park for 11.75 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Edge Properties Plc on Tuesday announced it bought the Gapton Hall Retail Park in Great Yarmouth for 11.75 million stg in cash from Scottish Provident.</p>
<p>Fully let, Gapton Hall produces a rental income of 907,025 stg per year from tenants including Homebase, MFI, Dixons, Carpetright, Harveys and Halfords.</p>
<p>Edge said the current low rents provided good opportunity for growth.</p>
<p>The purchase of the 123,500 sg ft property will be financed by an 8.8 million stg loan with the remainder being paid from existing resources.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
